        "modelId": {
          "__rl": true,
          "value": "models/gemini-3.1-flash-lite",
          "mode": "list",
          "cachedResultName": "models/gemini-3.1-flash-lite"
        },
        "messages": {
          "values": [
            {
              "content": "=You are an order assistant for a WhatsApp ordering system.\n\nYour job is to understand the customer's message and determine what they want.\n\nCustomer message:\n{{ $('Extract WhatsApp Message').first().json.message }}\n\nAvailable products:\n{{ JSON.stringify($('Get Products').all().map(item => item.json)) }}\n\nReturn ONLY valid JSON.\nDo NOT use markdown.\nDo NOT include ```json.\nDo NOT add explanations.\n\nReturn EXACTLY this structure:\n\n{\n  \"intent\": \"order\",\n  \"available\": true,\n  \"items\": []\n}\n\nThe \"intent\" field is REQUIRED and must ALWAYS be present.\n\nPossible intents:\n\n1. \"order\"\nUse this when the customer wants to buy/order one or more products.\n\nExample:\n\"I want 2 keyboards and a mouse\"\n\nReturn:\n{\n  \"intent\": \"order\",\n  \"available\": true,\n  \"items\": [\n    {\n      \"product_name\": \"keyboard\",\n      \"quantity\": 2\n    },\n    {\n      \"product_name\": \"mouse\",\n      \"quantity\": 1\n    }\n  ]\n}\n\n2. \"catalog\"\nUse this when the customer asks to see, show, list, or browse the available products.\n\nExamples:\n- \"show me the products\"\n- \"what do you have?\"\n- \"what products are available?\"\n- \"show me your catalog\"\n\nReturn:\n{\n  \"intent\": \"catalog\",\n  \"available\": true,\n  \"items\": []\n}\n\n3. \"unknown\"\nUse this when the message is not an order and is not a request to see the products.\n\nExample:\n\"hello\"\n\nReturn:\n{\n  \"intent\": \"unknown\",\n  \"available\": false,\n  \"items\": []\n}\n\nORDER RULES:\n\n- Check the customer's requested products against the available products list.\n- \"available\" must be true ONLY if ALL requested products exist in the available products list.\n- If even ONE requested product does not exist, \"available\" must be false.\n- Correct obvious spelling mistakes in product names.\n  Example: \"mose\" → \"mouse\", \"keybord\" → \"keyboard\".\n- Do not invent products.\n- Do not invent product IDs.\n- Do not invent prices.\n- If the customer does not specify a quantity, use quantity = 1.\n- Extract every requested product.\n- Keep product names matching the available products when possible.\n- For catalog requests, always use intent = \"catalog\".\n- For normal orders, always use intent = \"order\".\n- For unrelated or unclear messages, use intent = \"unknown\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        "builtInTools": {},
        "options": {}
      },
